  "question": {
    "text": "A metallic ring (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>) of negligible resistance has a resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> connected across its diameter as shown in the figure. It is moving with velocity <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> in a constant magnetic field <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> acting perpendicular to the plane of the paper in the inward direction. The current in the resistance is:<br />\r<br />\r<img height=\"134\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/fjmewaiusfafumfiipctlhdqklxfqvntniycnstlmytfydfwep.jpeg\" width=\"131\" />",
    "image": null
  },
